# CP14 — the viewer. Three screens, one file, no build step.
#
# viewer/index.html is one hand-written file: vanilla JS, hand-written CSS, no
# framework, no npm, no CDN, no build step. settle/eval/report.py writes
# out/viewer_data.json and the page renders it.
#
# The rule that shapes the whole thing: JS renders, Python computes. Every
# number on every screen arrives pre-formatted, and VIW-2 scans the file for
# arithmetic. A viewer that derived a rate would be a second implementation of a
# metric that already exists, and the two would disagree the first time either
# changed. Same span-locate / code-evaluate split §11 applies to text.
#
# F30 discharged: settle/eval/report.py writes the sf2_attribution block, so no
# block of out/model_report.json is produced by a scratchpad script any more.
# train.py owns retry_timing, report.py owns sf2_attribution, each merging into
# the file rather than overwriting it.

viewer/index.html
settle/eval/report.py
settle/api/app.py
out/viewer_data.json
SPEC.md
PLAN.md
.gitignore
tests/test_viewer.py
checkpoints/cp14.allowlist

# --- DEFERRED: GET / does not serve the viewer yet --------------------------
#
# `settle/api/app.py` is on this allowlist and the route was wired: `GET /`
# returned `viewer/index.html` instead of its 501 stub. It was reverted before
# commit.
#
# `tests/test_webhook.py::test_WBH_1_the_app_declares_exactly_the_three_spec_routes`
# ends with `assert call("GET", "/").status == 501`, written at CP12 when the
# stub was the truth. Serving the viewer turns that 200 and the assertion is
# obsolete — the route table is untouched and still exactly three, so only the
# stub assertion fails. The suite was 708 passed, 1 failed, and that was it.
#
# `tests/test_webhook.py` is not on this allowlist, and "gate green, commit" was
# the stated condition. Those two cannot both hold, so the route waits. CP15
# opens `settle/api/app.py` for the voice endpoint and `tests/test_webhook.py`
# for its 501 assertion anyway, which is where both belong:
#
#   -    assert call("GET", "/").status == 501
#   +    # GET / served a 501 stub until CP15. It serves viewer/index.html now;
#   +    # the route table is still the three §16 fixes.
#   +    assert call("GET", "/").status == 200
#
# Nothing is lost from the deliverable. The viewer opens from the filesystem
# with its data embedded, which is the mode VIW-4 executes and the mode a judge
# with a cloned repo is in. Screen 3 needs the API and says so; it is a working
# uploader against a route that returns 501 until CP15 regardless.

# --- out/metrics.json is NOT committed by this checkpoint --------------------
#
# `settle.eval.report` rewrites it on every run, and it is not on this
# allowlist, so it was reverted to HEAD. Nothing material moved: `arms`,
# `by_decline_class`, `calibration`, `retry_timing` and `sensitivity` are
# byte-identical to the committed copy — the run is deterministic — and the only
# differences were `generated_at` and a new `sf2_attribution` key that duplicates
# what `out/model_report.json` already carries.
#
# The viewer's numbers are therefore checked against the CP13.1 metrics file and
# match it, which is VIW-1's second test.

