# --- A note on the trace caps ------------------------------------------------
#
# 40 cases per arm plus any with a silent failure, and 8 decisions per case. A
# single OURS case holds thirty daily decisions each enumerating the whole
# action grid — 330 alternatives is normal — and sixty of those was a
# four-megabyte page.
#
# The alternatives inside a shown decision are never capped. Those are what
# VIW-3 is about, and a truncated option list is a decision log that has started
# lying. Decisions with a blocked option are kept first, because a gate stopping
# something the economics preferred is the most interesting row on the screen.
